tegic point along trade routes that connected Europe, the Middle East, and Asia, exemplifying the rich tapestry of cross-cultural exchanges that characterized the Early Modern period. Key figures such as the Persian Shah Abbas II and local tribal leaders influenced the city’s development, fostering a blend of cultures and economies.

